course: dictionary
lesson: 6322
title: A pattern that keeps coming back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A motif is a pattern, picture or idea that is repeated again and again. You can find motifs on a shirt, in a story and in a piece of music. «The vyshyvanka is the embroidered shirt, with regional patterns and colours.» The patterns on it are motifs, because the same shapes come back across the cloth.
explain: Use the context to find the meaning. Ask yourself: what keeps coming back here? In a story, a picture such as a storm that appears again and again is a motif. In music, a motif is a short group of notes that returns through a piece. Swap in "a repeated pattern or idea" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The meaning changes a little from place to place, but the idea of repeating stays the same. In art, you repeat a flower shape to make a pattern. In English, a writer repeats a symbol to show a theme. Both are motifs.
fact: A motif is a pattern, picture or idea that is repeated.
fact: «Some motifs have traditional meanings, while many are decoration and local style.» So a motif can be full of old meaning, or it can simply be decoration.
fact: «Vyshyvanka Day is in May.» A special day can celebrate a traditional shirt with its motifs.
fact: Phrases to know: a flower motif, a recurring motif (one that keeps coming back), and repeat the motif (do the same pattern again).
fact: In music, a motif is a short tune idea. It may be only a few notes, but it is repeated during the piece.
exercise: What is a motif? | A type of storm | A kind of shirt with long sleeves | *A pattern or picture that is repeated | A short, loud noise
exercise: In a story, the colour red keeps coming back again and again. What is that repeated colour called? | A full stop | *A motif | A rhyme | A question
exercise: «She printed the flower motif again and again on the tiles.» What does again and again show? | That she is tired | That the motif is very old | *That the motif is repeated | That the tiles are broken
test: In music, a short group of notes that is repeated in a piece is called a what? | *A motif | A chorus | A rest | A key
test: «Some motifs have traditional meanings, while many are decoration and local style.» What does this sentence tell us? | Motifs only appear in music | *Some motifs carry old meanings, and many are just decoration | All motifs are very old | Motifs are always sad
exam: Which sentence uses motif correctly? | The motif was a loud noise in the night | *The shirt had a bird motif that was repeated across the front | The motif ran very fast around the running track | I ate a motif for lunch
